 "drug_rule": "Doxepin is a weak inhibitor of CYP2D6 and CYP3A4. INH is partially metabolized by CYP2D6; inhibition can elevate INH plasma concentrations. Furthermore, both drugs independently prolong the QT interval, and their combined use may increase the risk of torsades de pointes, especially in patients with pre-existing cardiac vulnerability.",
