 "drug_rule": "Valacyclovir is primarily renally eliminated; dehydration reduces glomerular filtration, increasing the risk of valacyclovir accumulation and nephrotoxicity. High-dose ibuprofen can further impair renal function via prostaglandin-mediated afferent arteriolar vasoconstriction, compounding the risk. Additionally, valacyclovir is excreted unchanged in urine, and in a dehydrated state, peak concentrations may rise to toxic levels. Pregnancy in the third trimester also alters renal clearance and increases the risk of preterm labor or fetal distress if maternal toxicity occurs.",
