 "drug_rule": "Aminoglycosides are known to cause nephrotoxicity, often through the formation of complexes with renal tubular cells. Acyclovir, at high concentrations, can also induce renal tubular necrosis. In the presence of pre-existing renal impairment, the risk of additive nephrotoxicity is significantly elevated. The FDA label for valacyclovir warns against use in patients with severe renal impairment without dose adjustment, and aminoglycosides are contraindicated in moderate-to-severe renal impairment due to accumulation and toxicity.",
